  "authority": "docs/KARSIC_DIRECTORATE_STRUCTURE_PROGRAM.md#5-material-system",
  "notes": [
    "The generator never names a block. It names a role; this profile resolves the role to a block for the active stratum.",
    "Derivative naming is not uniform across this pack's mods. Immersive Engineering uses a PREFIX form (slab_concrete, stairs_concrete, wall_concrete); vanilla, Quark, TFMG and Supplementaries use a SUFFIX form. Both schemes are declared in derivative_schemes and resolved in that order.",
    "Roles that ARE a derivative (parapet_cap, stair_tread, coping) name the concrete block directly and declare no needs.",
    "A role only declares the derivative kinds the generator is actually allowed to request. Requiring derivatives a role never uses would fail the profile for no reason."
  ],
  "strata": ["K-I", "K-II", "K-III", "K-IV", "K-V"],
  "stratum_names": {
    "K-I": "Foundry Brick",
    "K-II": "First Standard",
    "K-III": "State Series",
    "K-IV": "Directorate Monumental",
    "K-V": "Late Retrofit"
  },
  "derivative_schemes": [
    "{ns}:{name}_{kind}",
    "{ns}:{singular}_{kind}",
    "{ns}:{kind}_{name}"
  ],

